extends RefCounted
## Main NPC line pools: 10 contexts x 4 lines = 40 each. Line id = "<context>_<n>".
## Contexts: greet farewell rich broke ugly sharp died boss idle buy
## The game picks the context from the player's state (see voice_lines.gd pick()).
## Story: Rico climbs five casinos (Atlantic Shitty -> Bellagiro) to win back his
## brother James from The House. Dark comedy; punchline last.

const POOLS := {
	"vera": {
		"greet": ["Sugar! Come in. I saved a charm for exactly your level of bad judgment.", "Sit down, sugar. The cards are warm, the incense is legal in most states, and my hope costs triple.", "Back again? Good. Everyone else in this building wants your soul. I only want your money.", "My crystal ball asked who keeps paying full price for hope. I said that's Rico, he's my college fund."],
		"farewell": ["Go climb, sugar. And if the House kills you, die near my shop. Funeral crowds buy a lot of candles.", "My charms work wonderfully, right up until they stop. I don't give refunds for stopping.", "Climb safe, sugar. You're my best customer, and dead customers leave terrible reviews.", "Walk toward the light, Rico. If you can't find it, walk toward my cash register."],
		"rich": ["Look at that wallet, sugar. It's begging me to take it, and I'm a woman who helps the needy.", "All that money and you came to see me? That's either wisdom or a cry for help, and both pay the same.", "You're glowing, sugar. Is that wealth or a medical issue? I'll sell you a charm for each.", "Rich suits you, Rico. It means you can afford the charms that come in a velvet bag with zero guarantees."],
		"broke": ["Broke, sugar? Fine. Hope is the only thing I sell that costs nothing to make, so I charge the most for it.", "You're not broke, sugar, you're pre-rich. It's a market segment, and I price it like one.", "Looking is free, sugar. Touching is a felony, and you've been eyeing that rabbit foot like a suspect.", "Come back when you've robbed someone with insurance. I'll sell you a charm that makes the police sleepy."],
		"ugly": ["Sugar, what are you wearing? That outfit looks like a hostage situation where the hostage lost.", "That outfit is cursed, darling. I'd know, I sell curses. Mine at least come in a nice box.", "Even the slot machines looked away when you walked in, and they don't have eyes.", "Go show Silas that outfit, honey. He'll faint, and I'm selling front row tickets with a free fainting charm."],
		"sharp": ["Now that's how you dress for a funeral, sugar. Your own. I love that you planned ahead.", "All dapper and doomed. I can't decide whether to read your future or just say you look pretty and take your money.", "You clean up nice, sugar. Try not to bleed on it, because no charm in this shop removes bloodstains.", "If you die in that suit, at least it's an open casket with taste. I'll bill you for the candle in advance."],
		"died": ["You died again, sugar. It's becoming a hobby, but I respect a man who commits to a bit.", "I saw it happen, honey. My shop cat watched too, then left the building without asking for a refund.", "Dust yourself off, sugar. You woke up owing more than before, so at least make that debt mean something.", "A bold way to lose, sugar. Not smart, just bold. In this town we put bold on the headstone and smart in the footnotes."],
		"boss": ["You beat a boss, sugar. I'll remember that fondly, right up until you owe me money in about three minutes.", "Another casino boss dethroned. I considered being nicer to you, then I remembered my prices.", "That boss had friends, sugar, mean wealthy ones. They'll be shopping for my most expensive curses, so thank you.", "Let me price that victory, sugar. To you it's a triumph. To me it's an upsell."],
		"idle": ["I keep telling the cards to stop gossiping about you, but they love a story that ends with someone losing everything.", "Everybody has a tell, Rico. Yours is hope, which is why I'll never stop selling it to you.", "Charms, curses and a little cold reading. The cold reading is just me watching you lose.", "Nobody who buys a lucky charm ever stops needing one. In the industry, we call that retention."],
		"buy": ["Wise choice, sugar. Or a terrible one. The fee's the same either way, so I'm thrilled.", "Take it, sugar, it likes you. It likes everyone. That's why I hired it.", "That charm bites a little, mostly in a good way. If it doesn't work, I'll gladly sell you another.", "Pleasure doing business, sugar. For me, a pleasure. For you, an educational experience."],
	},
	"fizz": {
		"greet": ["Psst, over here. Welcome to the pharmacy, which isn't licensed. I'm legally required to tell you that, then ask you to forget it.", "Come closer. Not that close, ugh, you breathe a lot. My products may cause drowsiness, euphoria, or a brief friendship with a paramedic.", "Welcome to Doc Fizz's. Every bottle has a legal warning, and today's is: please don't ask what the other bottle is for.", "A customer! Or a cop. Are you a cop? If so, this is a bakery and these are very strong muffins."],
		"farewell": ["Side effects begin immediately and last permanently. In rare cases you develop a French accent, which my warranty does not cover.", "Go on, be amazing. Statistically you'll be dead, but I'm told the amazing ones are really amazing.", "Keep the bottle. Do not return the bottle. It's been looking at me, and I'd rather not discuss what it said.", "Don't tell anyone where you got that. Especially me. Legally, I never met you."],
		"rich": ["You're loaded! Let me show you the good stuff, in the bag that hums. The warning on it is one I'm not allowed to read aloud.", "Real cash, my favorite! It tastes like a lawyer, and by law I must tell you the lawyer is also an ingredient.", "For you, double price and triple effect. Side effects now include, and I quote the form, a sudden urge to spend more money here.", "Hide that cash inside my product, it's the safest place. Warning: the product dissolves paper."],
		"broke": ["No cash? I accept organs. Small ones, spares really. You have spares, right? The form specifically says spares.", "Free sample! Free meaning my liability becomes your liability. By taking it, you also agree to be liable for my feelings.", "I'll put it on your tab, Rico. By tab I mean I'll bill your family. You have a family, right? I just invented one.", "Come back when you've been mugged by someone richer than you. At least then your wallet gets a better class of trauma."],
		"ugly": ["That outfit is a hallucination, and I haven't even sold you anything yet. Legal says that's somehow my fault.", "You look like a warning label, Rico, which I love. I write them. Mine are eight pages now.", "Don't worry about the outfit, the drugs make everything look better. A bottle once told me I'm very handsome in the right dose.", "I've seen better-fitting clothes on a cadaver, and I'm legally required to say the cadaver was not consulted."],
		"sharp": ["Fancy! That suit looks amazing until you spill something on it, and my products spill in six different colors.", "A well-dressed mistake, my favorite customer. They pay in cash and never read the label.", "You're too nice for this stall, Rico. Buy something. Side effects include a lowered moral baseline and a craving for shrimp.", "Sharp! Let's ruin it with science. Side effects include stains, glowing, and a mild urge to join a cult."],
		"died": ["You look dead, which means my product works. I have no data supporting that, other than your face.", "I heard the scream, and it was you. Nice lungs, by the way. That's a compliment, from a medical professional, sort of.", "Death isn't the problem, Rico, the respawn is. It's long, it's repetitive, and I'm told the loading screen is unbearable.", "Please don't die near the merchandise. The insurance covers nothing. I checked. The policy is a drawing of a duck."],
		"boss": ["You beat a boss! I need a pint of your blood for science. Okay, a gallon. I'm legally obligated to say it's not for science.", "You killed someone important, so celebrate with the red bottle. It's made from the last boss's leftovers, and the label says do not.", "Bosses are just customers who never paid their tab. Now I collect in trophies, and a little in organs.", "Did he have a kidney? Asking for business reasons. A second business, which I'm required to deny exists."],
		"idle": ["I have a bottle that sings. Badly. Mostly it screams, and screaming is a known side effect of the bottle.", "Everything has side effects, even oxygen. Ask anyone who's died of it. My labels are sixteen pages now, and the last four are apologies.", "Don't read the label, Rico. The label is lying. It's also a cousin of mine, which I'm required to disclose.", "Tell me your symptoms, then ignore my advice. That's the whole medical process here, and it has a ninety percent success rate, meaning you keep coming back."],
		"buy": ["Drink it fast. No, slow. Wait, fast. Whichever one you didn't do. I forgot which is safe, so it's a gamble either way.", "Side effects include luck, liver failure and a brief chat with a higher power. He says you owe him money too.", "Do not mix with alcohol, other medications, or the afternoon. If you must mix, do it far from my shop, my reputation and my dog.", "Good choice, probably. I don't read, I just pour and pray, and the prayer isn't responsible for the results either."],
	},
	"tailor": {
		"greet": ["Do come in, but mind the mannequins. They bite when ignored, and you look like someone who ignores things, including mirrors.", "Ah, a customer, or a stray. Hold still while I find out which, and don't breathe on the silk. It's older than your last three decisions combined.", "Silas Stitch, at your service. Good heavens, there's a lot of waistline here. We'll need the long tape, and possibly a second tailor.", "Welcome, welcome. Do sit down before you offend the mannequins. They have strong opinions about what you've chosen to wear."],
		"farewell": ["Wear it well, Rico. Or at least wear it. And whatever happens, never put it in a fanny pack.", "Mind the hem on the way out, and the door, and your life choices. Only one of those can be fixed by a tailor.", "Do try not to bleed on the silk, or the wool, or me. I have only one handkerchief and it's a rental.", "Come back for a fitting and a lecture. It's forty minutes long, it starts with your shoes, and it ends with your mother."],
		"rich": ["A gentleman with means! Now we can begin the long, lovely lie that you have taste, starting with a very expensive belt.", "Heavy pockets mean lovely hems. I'll bill you for both, and for the emotional labor of looking at you.", "With that fortune we might fix your posture, though I suspect surgery is the only honest option.", "Money, how delightfully vulgar. Spend it on me, and I'll make you a coat so fine the House will ask for my name."],
		"broke": ["No funds? Then we tailor in imagination. Imagine a very nice belt. There. That's two dollars.", "I can offer a belt of regret. It's free, it itches, and it clashes with everything, including your skin.", "Poverty is merely fashion in beta, darling. You've been in beta for years, and the reviews are devastating.", "Come back when you can afford sleeves, my dear. Until then you're a vest, and a tragic one, but at least well ventilated."],
		"ugly": ["Dear boy, did you dress yourself in a dumpster? Don't answer. The smell already did.", "That fanny pack is a war crime. I'd gladly testify, in my best suit, the only thing here you haven't offended.", "I won't say what I think. I will faint instead. Watch. There. Now I need water and a different customer.", "You look like a rumor of an outfit, Rico, and a poorly sourced one. Even my mannequins have turned to face the wall."],
		"sharp": ["Now that is a proper silhouette, Rico. A murder suspect, but a dapper one, and I'd happily testify to the tailoring.", "Magnificent. I'd hang it in a museum, next to the exhibit of men who died wearing it. It's a very popular wing.", "You're a credit to the craft, Rico, and to my commission. In a rare moment of sincerity, I may even stop judging your shoes.", "I made half that outfit. You made the other half, barely. Squint and it almost works, and I'm taking all the credit."],
		"died": ["You died in my wares, Rico? Did it stain? I can fix a hole, but I cannot fix a blood type.", "A dead client is a quiet client, which I love. A bloody client is a lawsuit, and my lawyer is a mannequin.", "Bleed on the old stock if you must, but never the new silk. I promised that silk a better life.", "Hold still, I'll mend the holes. Which are bullet holes and which are style? Don't tell me. I prefer to think they're all style."],
		"boss": ["You defeated a boss, how marvelous. Then you'll need armor, fashionable armor. Is there any other kind? No.", "Slaying monsters in silk, how delightful. Stains come out with lemon, wine and prayer, in that order, and the prayer is mostly for me.", "Those trophies will need a tasteful frame, Rico, and perhaps a better class of enemy. One who dresses with intention.", "I once made that boss a custom suit. He hated it. Now he's dead, so technically I got the last word."],
		"idle": ["Gloves for gripping, boots for smashing, scarves for gliding. Hats are for nothing. I simply like hats.", "The shoes make the man, Rico. I just wish the man would hold still for a fitting.", "Stand straight, Rico. The cloth knows. It's judging your spine, and it is extremely disappointed.", "Everything I sell grants a talent, mostly vanity, occasionally a double jump. I've never decided which is more useful in this building."],
		"buy": ["A fine choice. I knew it would suit you. I say that to everyone and it's never true, but this time it's slightly less false.", "Wear it with confidence, Rico, or at least with shoes. I'm still not convinced you own any.", "I shall tell the thread you said hello. The thread has opinions about you, and none are flattering.", "One moment while I finish. The pins are my pride, and also my weapons, and I won't discuss the second part with the authorities."],
	},
	"gunny": {
		"greet": ["Welcome to the armory, recruit. Say hello to Betsy, the shotgun on the left. She never likes anyone, so I'm a little jealous.", "Stand up straight, recruit. You're in the presence of firepower, and I'm not talking about me. I'm talking about the lady on the wall. Stop staring, you're making her blush.", "You need firepower, recruit. I can smell it on you. I can also smell that you need a shower, but that's not in stock.", "Welcome, gambler. Everything in here goes bang, and nothing goes whimper. Unlike your bankroll."],
		"farewell": ["Don't shoot your own foot, recruit. Shoot theirs. Betsy hates it when you mix those up.", "Dismissed. Try to die facing forward. Backward deaths mean paperwork, and Betsy cries over paperwork.", "Clean your guns, wash your hands, but never wash the lucky socks. They're load-bearing.", "Move out, rookie, and don't bet the ammo. I've named every bullet in that box, and I get attached."],
		"rich": ["Cash! The universal caliber! Listen, Betsy's purring. She hasn't purred since the divorce.", "A big spender. I salute your wallet. If I could marry it, I'd have to ask Betsy first, and she's protective.", "Now I'll show you the good stuff, recruit. Treat her right. She's like a daughter to me, in a way my lawyer has asked me to stop describing.", "That's purchasing power. I'm throwing in a free clip and a long moment alone with the new shotgun. Don't watch."],
		"broke": ["No money, no bang. Oldest rule in the armory, and also the plot of your whole life.", "Broke? Throw rocks. Rocks have a perfect safety record, if you ignore that glacier incident.", "Hands off the shelves, recruit. Betsy doesn't like being touched by people who can't afford her.", "No cash? You can look. But Betsy sees you staring, and she says buy her or stop breathing on the glass."],
		"ugly": ["Soldier, that outfit is a disciplinary action. I've seen less offensive things come out of a mortar.", "Camouflage? You look like a bruise wandering around. Betsy sighed when you walked in, and she never sighs.", "I've seen better uniforms on a scarecrow, recruit. The scarecrow had a better stance, a stronger sense of purpose, and honestly a nicer rifle.", "What happened to your pants, recruit? If the House took them, I'd like to report it. If you picked them, I'd like to report that too."],
		"sharp": ["Spit-shined, recruit. I'm almost proud. Don't tell Betsy. She thinks she's my favorite.", "That suit says lethal in four languages. Shame you only speak panic.", "A sharp dresser holds a gun better. Scientific fact. The guns agree. They find you attractive, which is honestly unsettling.", "You look like a general, recruit. So act like one: send others to die first and keep the good guns for yourself."],
		"died": ["You're dead? Walk it off, recruit. And do it away from Betsy, she just had her stock polished.", "That's what armor is for, recruit. You forgot yours. Again. I keep handing you new ones like a patient father, and you keep feeding them to the floor.", "Retrain, rearm, resurrect, repeat. That's the whole military, and also your career.", "The only bad death is an unarmed death, recruit, and yours was a very unarmed one. Betsy would like a word."],
		"boss": ["Boss down! Medals for everyone except the boss, who gets a closed casket. Betsy gets a fresh coat of oil. She earned it.", "That boss was large, loud, and legally ambiguous. Exactly what my ex-wife called me, and I took it as a compliment.", "I sold that boss his first revolver. I regret nothing, except his trigger discipline. That one's on me.", "You beat a boss, recruit, and I got a little misty. Betsy saw. We're not discussing it."],
		"idle": ["I'm naming the new shotgun and I need your opinion. Marjorie or Danielle? She's sensitive, so choose carefully.", "A revolver has six reasons, recruit. Use five. Save one for the barista. He knows what he did.", "The coin shotgun is my favorite. It's illegal in four countries and one Pizza Hut. I miss that Pizza Hut every day.", "Guns don't kill people, recruit, bad odds do. And Gary. We don't talk about Gary, and neither does Betsy."],
		"buy": ["Excellent choice, recruit. Point it away from yourself, me, and Betsy. She's sensitive about being aimed at.", "Classic. Respect it. It's seen things, mostly foreheads.", "Eight out of ten customers survive their first purchase. You're a nine, which is mathematically impossible, and Betsy agrees.", "Be gentle with her, recruit. She kicks. If she makes a sound, that's just the love."],
	},
	"lucky": {
		"greet": ["Sit anywhere but the stool by the door, runner. The pool says you die there, and I've got money on it.", "The usual? Take your time ordering. I've got ten bucks on you dying mid-sentence, and I want to enjoy it.", "Welcome to Lucky's. We don't water the drinks much, and the pool on how you die is up to six hundred.", "You're breathing! I had you at even money not to. I lost, and I've never been happier. Don't tell the pool."],
		"farewell": ["Drink responsibly, runner. Or at least drink first. I'll keep a stool warm and the pool open on how you leave.", "Come back in one piece. Or two, I'm not picky. I have a mop, and I have money on which.", "Break a leg out there, runner. I've got twenty on left leg, first floor. No pressure.", "I'll keep your tab open. It's the only thing here that never closes. The pool closes at midnight."],
		"rich": ["First round's on me, second's on you, third's on your fortune. The pool says you'll lose it all by dinner.", "That's a lot of green, runner. I've got a Scotch that'll make you cry, and six guys in the pool who'll cry harder if you keep it.", "Cash like that needs a toast and an alibi. I'll do the toast. The guys in the pool sell alibis.", "You're buying, aren't you? I'm already pouring. I've moved the pool to 'dies drunk and rich,' and it's a crowd favorite."],
		"broke": ["Tab's on me tonight, runner. Don't make it a habit, make it a hobby. The pool's offering you ten percent if you die before closing.", "I'll pour you water, runner. It's all I've got that's free, and I'm not totally sure it's honest.", "Broke? Join the club. Dues are one drink per sorrow, and you owe me nine years.", "Sit, runner, cry, hydrate. The tears are on the house. The guys in the pool are betting on how long you last without a drink."],
		"ugly": ["That outfit's strong, runner, like my worst whiskey. You smell about the same. I've got a pool on which one knocks someone out first.", "I've seen better coats in the lost and found. They were on fire, and still more flattering.", "Not my business what you wear, runner. But I've added 'death by fashion' to the pool, and it's paying well.", "Have a drink, runner. It blurs everything, and I'd like that for both of us."],
		"sharp": ["Look at you, runner. All class, no chaser. Wait, I have chasers. Good. The pool now has 'best dressed corpse,' and you're the front-runner.", "Dressed to kill, or at least to be killed in. I've got forty bucks on the second one.", "That suit deserves a good Scotch. You get the cheap one. Fair's fair.", "You almost look like you belong here, runner. One drink fixes that. Two makes the pool very interesting."],
		"died": ["Welcome back, runner. I had you dying on the stairs, so thank you. Drinks are on the guy who bet 'spikes.' He's very upset.", "Rough one, runner. I had you picked for the elevator, so now I owe a man in a hat forty bucks. He's smug about it. Take that personally.", "You died, runner, so have a drink. It won't help, but it gives your hands something to do. The pool just paid out, so it's on me.", "That's death number forty-three, runner. I had 'ugly and sudden,' so I'm buying a round for myself."],
		"boss": ["You beat a boss, runner? Round's on me. I had you dying to him, and now I owe the whole bar.", "Cheers to the one that fell. May he rest, and may his tab be forgiven. It won't be.", "That boss drank here, runner. Tipped badly, died worse. I'd say rest in peace, but he owes me for eleven Scotches.", "A toast to the one who didn't die tonight, runner. Tonight being relative. I've already got money on tomorrow."],
		"idle": ["I've got a bar on every floor, runner. It's convenient. You die, I'm already there to collect.", "The pool on how many times you die before the Bellagiro is at fifty-three. The guy who bet sixty is crying.", "A drink never lies, runner. Only the drinker does. And the bartender, but don't ask him, he's me.", "My whole job is wiping a glass and listening, runner. Mostly I listen for the thud. It's how I settle the pool."],
		"buy": ["Bottoms up, runner. Gently, like a bad idea. I've got a bet on how long you keep it down, and the odds are not in your favor.", "That one has a kick, runner. I've got ten bucks on whether you stay standing after it.", "Careful, runner, don't spill it. I'll bet you ten bucks you do. Actually, make it twenty. I know you.", "On the house, runner. Not THE House, that one never pays. The pool covers it. The pool loves you."],
	},
	"mags": {
		"greet": ["Rico, sweetheart, my favorite investment! You look terrible, which is wonderful news for my interest rate.", "I was just counting your debt, kid. It's gotten so big, and I swear it has your eyes. I'm keeping it as a pet.", "Sit, sit. Standing's fine too, for now. I'm lenient on the first visit, and I only bite on the second. By bite, I mean charge.", "Kid, you're on time! I love that. Late is where the bodies are buried, and I don't want to dig again."],
		"farewell": ["Don't make me swim after you, Rico. I just did my hair. I'll do it, sweetie, but I'll be cross.", "Pay me, sweetie, or I'll collect. I say it with so much love. And a little with teeth.", "Be careful out there, kid. It would be such a waste. Of my time, I mean. Mostly my time.", "Go on, sweetie. Buttons and I will wait up. He's practicing his growl for when you're late."],
		"rich": ["Look at all that money, Rico. It looks so lonely. Let me adopt it. I have room and a very large tank.", "You could pay me early, sweetie. Nobody ever has. I'd faint, and then I'd get suspicious.", "Money, my favorite snack! Hold it for me, Rico. Just near my mouth.", "A big pot, sweetheart, so I'd love to borrow a little. The way a shark borrows a swimmer."],
		"broke": ["Broke, sweetie? I'll float you a loan. A shark does take care of its fish, right up until dinner.", "Empty pockets and so much potential, kid. All of it mine.", "I never judge, Rico. I only remember every missed payment. Buttons remembers too, and he's been looking at your ankles.", "Broke is just a loan that hasn't happened yet, sweetheart. Come here. I'll make it happen."],
		"ugly": ["That outfit is a loan officer's nightmare, Rico. I want it framed, for the days I need to feel better about my life.", "Sweetie, I'd lend you a better suit, but you'd never give it back, and I'd have to collect it off you.", "Is that a fanny pack, Rico? I'm calling your mother. Then I'm introducing her to the debt.", "I've collected from better-dressed corpses, kid. And they paid faster."],
		"sharp": ["Nice suit, kid. Looks expensive, and I know exactly whose money that is. It's mine. It looks better on you.", "Dressed to impress, sweetheart. I'm impressed. Now pay up, and I'll let you keep the cufflinks.", "That's a lot of my money on your back, Rico. I'll take a cut. Starting with the shoulders.", "Now you look like a lender, kid. Careful. I eat my competition."],
		"died": ["You died, sweetie, so I'm adding it to your interest. Death is a surcharge. Think of it as a little gift to me.", "No refunds in the afterlife, Rico. I'd know. I've got a branch there, with a lovely view, staffed by your debt.", "Dead men don't pay, kid, but they do borrow. It's one of my best markets.", "Death is just a very late payment, sweetheart. Either way, you end up with me, and I'll be waiting with a pen."],
		"boss": ["A boss, defeated? Wonderful. His debts are mine now, and so is his dog. I don't want the dog. Bring it anyway.", "Take your spoils, Rico, and I'll take my share. The law has a different word for it, but the law is just jealous.", "Winning's expensive, sweetheart. Let me carry it for you. In my teeth.", "You beat the boss, kid. Now beat the interest. Good luck. Nobody has, and I invented it."],
		"idle": ["Don't think of it as debt, sweetie. Think of it as a relationship. A deep one, with teeth.", "I like you, Rico, and that's the problem. I like everything I eat.", "Everybody owes somebody, kid. I just own the paperwork, the walls, the floor, and a bit of your left kidney.", "I swim every day, sweetheart. Just in case you ever run."],
		"buy": ["Sign here, and here, and here. Don't read it, kid. Nobody reads it, and I find that so romantic.", "A pleasure, Rico. I'll bill you later. Wait, I already did. I love having you as a customer.", "Smart, kid. Debt is just future money you spent early. Think of it as time travel with teeth.", "No refunds, sweetheart. But I do accept regrets as payment, and you have such a lovely collection."],
	},
	"marlow": {
		"greet": ["Rico, you picked up. I bet against that, so I owe myself money. Typical.", "Marlow here. Talk fast. The sandwich is getting cold and so is my will to live.", "Back already, kid? I was just worrying about you. It's my only hobby, besides guilt.", "Say something stupid so I know you're alive. Perfect. Now I can go back to feeling guilty about James."],
		"farewell": ["Stay alive, stay lucky, or stay on the line. Pick two. I've never managed even one.", "Call me if you need me, kid. Call me if you don't. It's a payphone, nobody else does.", "Don't do anything I'd worry about. Too late, I've started the eulogy. It's mostly about me.", "Go get your brother, Rico. The one I got the seat for. I really hate how that sentence ends."],
		"rich": ["You're rich, Rico. Bank it. Please. I'm begging from the floor, where I've been lying down since the last time you were rich.", "Don't tell the House you're rich, and for the love of God, don't tell James. He'll want a loan.", "Bank it, Rico, please. I'm on the floor begging. The dust bunny and I are on a first-name basis.", "I've seen men lose that much in one hand, kid. Twice it was me. Once it was your brother, and I helped."],
		"broke": ["Broke again? That's three times today, and it's lunch. Your brother budgets better, and he lives in a casino.", "It's just money, Rico, it comes back. Probably. I'm a bad promise guy, ask James.", "I'd cover dinner, but I'm broke too, and James still thinks I'm solvent. Don't tell him.", "You're not broke, Rico, you're liquid. Sad, like a puddle. Same energy as me, except I have a sandwich."],
		"ugly": ["What are you wearing, Rico? I'm on a payphone and I can still hear it whisper 'help.'", "Is that a fanny pack? Don't ask how I can see it. Some things you feel through the phone.", "Style isn't everything, Rico. It's about eighty percent. I got through life on the other twenty, which is why I live in a phone booth.", "Please go see Silas, kid. I'm in a phone booth. There's nowhere to look but you."],
		"sharp": ["Nice suit, Rico. I can hear the starch. It's screaming 'don't bleed on me.'", "You look like a man with a plan. Do you have a plan? Blink twice if no. Right, it's a phone.", "Dressed to kill, kid. Please try not to be killed in it. Silas would never forgive either of us.", "Nice threads, Rico. Keep the blood off. I called in favors for that fabric, and I'm out of favors and friends."],
		"died": ["Rico, again? We have to stop meeting like this: you dead, me on a payphone, a sandwich in the middle.", "I heard the thud, kid. I clapped before I could stop myself. Now I feel terrible and I'm eating about it.", "You died, so I lit a candle. It's a matchstick. Don't make it weird, it's what I can afford.", "Good news, you're alive again. Bad news, it's still me on the phone, and James is still in there."],
		"boss": ["Boss down? I'm updating my bet. I now say you survive. First time I've bet on you. Put it in writing so I can't back out.", "One casino down, kid. James is a little closer. Or farther. I'm checking the map, by which I mean a napkin.", "You did it, Rico. Don't let it go to your head. Let it go to the bank. I'll have a sandwich ready.", "I'm proud of you, kid. I'm checking my pulse. Pride and a pulse in one afternoon, I might die."],
		"idle": ["Five casinos, twenty-five floors, and James at the top of the Bellagiro. Easy. By easy I mean impossible. I'm sorry.", "I keep thinking about the day I got James that seat. I tell myself it was a favor. Then I eat.", "Follow the light, kid. Hopefully it's the exit and not the one people see at the end. Call me either way.", "Every floor has a story, Rico. Yours are all about losing. Mine is about a payphone, a sandwich, and one bad favor."],
		"buy": ["Good call, kid. Not great. Good, like a report card for a goldfish. I'm celebrating with a small sandwich.", "Read the fine print, Rico. There's no fine print. That's the fine print. I should know, I signed everything, including your brother's seat.", "I wouldn't. But I'm not you, thank God. I'm saying that with guilt and some mayo.", "James would have bought that too. Look where it got him. Actually, look where it got me. I'm the one who feels bad."],
	},
	"james": {
		"greet": ["Rico! Great timing, I'm up. Give me one more hand and we'll catch up. Don't sit down, they recruit.", "I knew you'd come, Rico. I had money on never, but I'm winning, so no hard feelings.", "Oh, it's you. I thought you were the dealer. Same energy, though. One more hand, then we hug.", "What day is it, Rico? Is there a day? Anyway, I'd love to catch up, right after this hand."],
		"farewell": ["Don't wait for me, Rico. I'm busy being a legend. I'll be out after one more hand. Probably two.", "Tell Mom I'm doing great. She'll ask for her money back. Tell her I'm doing great about that too.", "Take the chips, leave the cards. And the chair. I'm very attached to the chair.", "Come back anytime, Rico. I'll be here. I'm always here. That's not a problem, that's a schedule."],
		"rich": ["That's a lot of chips, Rico. Don't trust them. They're sparkly liars. Mine love me, though.", "I had that much once, for ten minutes. Best ten minutes of my life. I've been chasing them for three years.", "Bank it, Rico? Sure, bank it. Or spend it at my table. We have a very nice table.", "Being rich didn't help me, Rico. It just changed how I lost. Now I lose in a nicer chair."],
		"broke": ["Broke, Rico? Welcome. It's cozy. The rent's nothing, and the walls are close enough to hug.", "I've been broke three years, Rico. It's great. You find a lot of hobbies. Mine is staying right here.", "It's just money, Rico. It was never ours, it's the House's. I'm only borrowing my own future, and they're very flexible about it.", "Broke together, Rico. That's called family. Or a pyramid scheme. Want in? I get a commission."],
		"ugly": ["Nice outfit, Rico. I love it. I'm lying. I'm in a good mood, so it's a happy lie.", "I'd say something, Rico, but you're my brother. So I'll just say it quietly, with my eyes.", "You look like me after three years at the table. Is that a stain? Oh, that one's mine. Keep it.", "Mom would cry, then laugh, then ask where you got it, then cry again. It's her whole routine for me."],
		"sharp": ["You look great, Rico. Who died? If it's me, nobody told me, and I'm right here.", "Dad would be proud, Rico. Then he'd ask where you stole it. Then he'd borrow it.", "I used to dress like that, Rico. Now I wear the House's vest. It has a name tag. I love the name tag.", "Did you buy that with my debts? It's got my fingerprints on it. Fine, keep it. Looks better on you."],
		"died": ["You died? Welcome to my life, Rico. It's less dead than you'd think, but more paperwork.", "It stops hurting after the first twenty, Rico. Then it's just paperwork. I do a lot of paperwork here. I love it.", "I've died at this table a hundred times, Rico. You get used to it. The lighting's flattering.", "Get up, Rico. It's just a body. Mine's been on layaway for years, and I'm fine."],
		"boss": ["I never got past the third boss, Rico. Then I found the table, and honestly, I stopped needing to.", "I heard the table go quiet. That was you, or the building collapsing. Either way, I'm still seated.", "The House notices everything, Rico. It noticed me twice, and now I have a name tag and a very small pension.", "I'm proud of you, Rico. And scared. And jealous. Mostly jealous. Please lose a little, for me."],
		"idle": ["The cards remember everything, Rico. Especially the bad hands. We're very close.", "You hear that wheel, Rico? It never stops. It also never says sorry. I find that very honest.", "I counted every floor, Rico. There's more. It's a growing business, and I'm basically a founding member.", "Be careful with the House, Rico. It's not a person. It's a vibe with lawyers. A vibe I work for."],
		"buy": ["Good pick, Rico. I'd have picked it too. I lost anyway, but with style.", "Don't buy it, Rico. ... You bought it. That's exactly how I got my table.", "It might work. Mine didn't. But I'm an optimist, which is just a gambler who's still sitting down.", "At least you're trying, Rico. That's what everyone said at my intervention. Great snacks, though."],
	},
	"rico": {
		"greet": ["Let's see what the House left me. Not my brother, not my dignity. Oh, nice, one chip.", "Aces up, brains out. Perfect strategy. The House calls it 'our customer profile.'", "Another day, another dollar I don't have. At least I'm consistent. That's called momentum.", "Let it ride, baby! Or fold. I'm indifferent. I'm lying, LET IT RIDE."],
		"farewell": ["Wish me luck. Please. I'm asking a vending machine, so yeah, it's that bad.", "See you at the top of the Bellagiro, or the bottom of a dumpster. Same dress code.", "I'll be rich by dinner, or dead by dinner. Either way I'm skipping the check.", "Let it ride. And if it doesn't, I respawn with a better last line."],
		"rich": ["I'm rich. Wait, let me count again. That's one chip. Fine, still rich.", "Look at all this money. Time to bet it all. It's the responsible thing. I'm using the word wrong, on purpose.", "Cash out? I don't even know her.", "The pot's fat, so I'll make it fatter. Then I'll lose it. Balance matters."],
		"broke": ["Broke means I have nothing to lose. Which has never once stopped me from losing it.", "Zero dollars, infinite possibilities. Mostly pawn shops. Mags is going to love this.", "I've been broker than this. I'm fine. Look, I'm doing a little dance. It's mostly shaking.", "Rock bottom has a great view of other, deeper bottoms."],
		"ugly": ["I look like a dumpster fire, and I love it. Fire's warm. Dumpsters are home.", "Is this fanny pack lucky? Please be lucky. I'm begging a fanny pack. New low.", "Style is for people with good odds. I have vibes, and I wear them to every boss fight.", "Somebody call a stylist. Or an exorcist. Or a stylist who's an exorcist. I pay in future winnings."],
		"sharp": ["I look incredible. The House should be scared. And then it should add this suit to my tab.", "Dressed to kill, or at least to lose in style. Style is the only thing I keep.", "I clean up nice. Just don't look at the shoes. The shoes are doing their best.", "Would I bet on me looking this good? Obviously. I already put the suit on credit."],
		"died": ["Okay, that one was on me. The last one was the wall's fault. The one before that was also the wall.", "Dying is no big deal. I do it for a living. A bad living, but still. The loading screen knows my name.", "Next time I'll do it differently. Or exactly the same. Variety is overrated.", "I regret nothing. Except that. And the thing before it. And, okay, the whole year."],
		"boss": ["Read 'em and weep, pal. You're weeping already? Good. I'll send flowers to your next of kin, the House.", "Another boss down, another reason to gamble. Not that I ever needed one.", "I called the bluff, and then the bluff cried. Unprofessional. Ten out of ten.", "Who's next? Don't tell me. Okay, tell me, but make it dramatic."],
		"idle": ["Odds are for people with a plan. I have a hunch and a bus pass.", "I once bet my shoes. Won them, lost them, walked home barefoot. Net zero shoes, but I felt incredible.", "Risk is just fun with consequences. The consequences are mostly a rash.", "The plan: climb five casinos, get James, don't bet him. Step three is going to be the hard part."],
		"buy": ["Take my money! Wait, all of it? Fine, take all of it.", "Sold. Wait, what was the price? Never mind, sold. James would be so proud. That's the problem.", "Worth it, probably. If I die, it's a donation to people with fewer problems. So, anybody.", "That's a terrible deal. I'm in. I'm so in. I was in before you finished the sentence."],
	},
}
